	title 'DefProcs'************************************************************************ Control Manager Def Procs** Copyright (C)* Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-1992* All Rights Reserved** 28 Sep 88	Steven Glass** Change in the way that the recsize routines can use the param* field.  If the routines are called by NewControl, param is zero.* If the routines are called by NewControl2, param is pointer to* template.** Added code to nor_size to see what kind of control is being built.* When the control is super, it sees if the title or color table must* be included in the control record when determining the size.** Added code to simp_init to init the fields that are not inited* by NewControl2** Added simp_disp to release any resources accessed by the def_proc.** 18 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Check Invis bit in each draw routine:**	simp_draw*	check_draw*	radio_draw*	grow_draw*	scroll_draw** Only draw if bit is clear.** 07 Dec 88	Steven Glass** PCount test in InitScroll was wrong.** 19 Dec 88	Steven Glass** In order to get the setup of the ColorPtr removed from the* standard start drawing routines, I've put it into this* file.  Every entry point that leads to drawing now must* have a call to setupColor in it.  ** Moreover, all references to the color table after* setup color must be made before any call that can move* memory.** Sure hope this works.** 22 Feb 89	Harry Yee** Dimming done on a simple button is different from dimming for any* of the other standard controls. We were not checking the right flags* to determine whether the control was a simple button or not therefore* we were always dimming a control that was rectangular. Once we've* determined that a control is a simple button we must also check whether* its a rectangular or round button. If rectangular than dimming is done* the same as that for other controls. BRC #44356.** Modified MoveThumb routine. The colorptr was not being set up at the * right place. SetUpColor which sets up <colorptr was being called at* a place that could get branched around. This caused problems because* draw_thumb, which always gets called expects <colorptr to be set up. ** 28 Mar 89	Steven Glass** All defProcs now support the new ctlWinstateChange message.  All in* this file just inval their ctlRects.*** 05 Apr 89	Dave Good** The scroll bar and grow box defprocs now call the correct routine* to invalidate their rects (they used to just jump to an rts).** 06 Apr 89	Harry Yee** Fix bug in grow box control init routine (init_grow). We use to just check* the middle byte of the ctlColor field to see if the default color table* should be used. If the ctlColor field was a resource ID then there was a* good chance that the middle byte would be zero (i.e. ID = 1) and the ptr* to the default color table would overwrite the resource ID. We now check* to make the sure the high and low byte of ctlColor is zero before using* the default.** For buttons, radio buttons, and check boxes that use resources for their* color table we were not releasing the color resource correctly. Fixed.** 07 Apr 89	Harry Yee** The Check box and radio button icon would not draw correctly if the control* used a resource for its color table. In routine radio_check the x-reg comes* set to value that tells the routine with icon to draw. Routine SetupColor* was trashing the x-reg before it got used if the color table happened to be* a resource. We now save the value of <x> on the stack before calling SetupColor.* WorkSheet #BCOJHS099. ** 28 Apr 89	Harry Yee** Changed routine Radio_Check. The width of the radio button icon was not being* set up correctly because routine get_csize requires the x-reg to be setup when * its called, which it wasn't. Going into routine get_csize x-reg was always zero. * Therefore when we drew the title we were calculating the x start position using * the width for a check box icon (which is icon number 0) instead of a radio * button icon.** 4-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Changed scroll bar NewValue routine (move_thumb) to delay until minScrollTicks* have passed since the last scroll bar NewValue message.  This maxes out the* scrolling speed for souped-up machines.** 6-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Changed the scroll bar delay thing to use WaitUntil in misc tools.** 21-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Added a missing SEC in draw_icon (for scroll bar bug).** 9-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Scroll_init calls CtlNewRes to force computation of the new pattern/color* for the thumb area (gray if available, checkerboard if not).** Scroll_draw checks bit 6 of the scroll bar's ctlFlag; if set, the bar* is part of an extended list control (handle in the refcon), so it calls* CallCtlDefProc and feeds the list the ctlChangeTarget message so that* the focus frame is always redrawn.** 9-Jan-92	Dave Lyons** Set a valid port around the CtlNewRes call in the scroll bar defproc.** 6-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Scroll bar preserves [<data],State around CallCtlDefProc when notifying* an extended List control to redraw the focus frame.***********************************************************************	string asis	blanks off	print push	print off	include 'all.macros'	include 'equates.asm'	include 'superequates.asm'	include 'e16.event'	print pop	title 'SIMP_PROC';====================================================================;;          Main line Simple Button handler.;;   IN:    a = task.;          Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          param = additional parameter.;;  OUT:    a = low word of returned value.;          x = high	word of returned value.;;====================================================================simp_proc 	proc EXPORT	cmp #ctlWinStateChange+1	Ignore any messages out of range	bcs null_ret	asl a	Compute index for dispatch.	tax	lda >simp_tasks,x	pha	ldx #$FFFF	Simple buttom number.	rts	Complete the task.;simp_tasks	DC.W simp_draw-1	0 Draw simple button.	DC.W null_ret-1	1 Compute drag RECT.	DC.W test_butt-1	2 Common hit test routine.	DC.W simp_init-1	3 Initialize the control.	DC.W simp_disp-1	4 Dispose.	DC.W simp_draw-1	5 New value.	DC.W null_ret-1	6 Compute Thumber constrains.	DC.W null_ret-1	7 Drag the indicator.	DC.W null_ret-1	8 Auto action.	DC.W simp_draw-1	9 New value.	DC.W null_ret-1	10 Set min max.	DC.W null_ret-1	11 Move button.	DC.W nor_size-1	12 Return size of standard record.	dc.W nor_event-1	13 Handle events	dc.W null_ret-1	14 ctlChangeTarget	dc.W null_ret-1	15 ctlChagneBounds	dc.W null_ret-1	16 ctlWindChagneSize	dc.W null_ret-1	17 ctlHandleTab	dc.W null_ret-1	18 ctlNotifyMultiPart	dc.W Inval_rect-1	19 ctlWinStateChange (just inval)	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Return Null;;====================================================================null_ret	proc EXPORT;	lda #0	Nothing flag.	tax		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          nor_event;;====================================================================nor_event	proc EXPORT	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlHilite	lda [ctlPtr],y	and #$00FF	cmp #$00FF	beq DontWantIt	ldy #oWhat	lda [param],y	cmp #keyDownEvt	beq TryThisOne	cmp #autoKeyEvt	bne DontWantItTryThisOne;; Start with the modifiers.;	ldy #oModifiers		; Look at the high byte	lda [param],y		; of the modifiers	and #$FF00	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlKeyModsCareBits	; and with the care bits	and [ctlPtr],y	dey		; compare with the desired mods	dey	cmp [ctlPtr],y	bne DontWantIt;; If we get to here, then the mods matched.  So look at the key.;	dey	dey	lda [ctlPtr],y	tax	and #$00FF		; first look at key1	ldy #oMessage	cmp [param],y	beq WantIt	txa		; now try key2	xba	and #$00FF	cmp [param],y	bne DontWantItWantIt	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+3	lda [ctlPtr],y	and #$007F	tax	lda >WhichPart,x	pha	pei ctlHand+2	pei ctlHand	_HiliteControl	PushWord #0	pei ctlHand+2	pei ctlHand	_HiliteControl	lda #$FFFF	Return true for having handled event	tax	rtsDontWantIt	lda #0	Return False, don't want event.	tax		rtsWhichPart	dc.w 2	; button offset is 0, part is 2	dc.w 3	; check offset is 2, part is 3	dc.w 4	; radio offset is 4, part is 4	ENDP;====================================================================;;          simp_disp;; releases any resources used by the control;;====================================================================simp_disp	proc EXPORT	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	bpl NeverMind	jsr ReadMoreFlags	and #TitleVerbMask	cmp #TitleIsResource	bne TitleNotResource	PushWord #rString	jsr CtlDataToAX	phx	pha	jsr ReleaseResourceTitleNotResource	jsr ReadMoreFlags	and #ColorTableVerbMask	cmp #ColorTableIsResource	bne CTNotResource	PushWord #rCtlColorTable	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlColor+2	lda [<Ctlptr],y	pha	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlColor	lda [<Ctlptr],y	pha	jsr ReleaseResourceCTNotResourceNeverMind	lda #0	tax	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Return size of required record.;;====================================================================nor_size	proc EXPORT	lda param	ora param+2	bne EeeGads	lda #CtlColor+4	Size of standard control record.	ldx #0	High word of size.		rtsEeeGads	lda #SuperCtlSize	ldx #0	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Initialize simple button.;;   IN:    x = $FFFF to initialize a simple buttom.;          x = zero	to initialize check	box.;          x = 4 to	initialize radio button.;          Ctlptr =	control pointer.;; NewControl set all the fields but some defaults need ; expansion.;; NewControl2 requires that the same fields be expanded; and the indicated fields be set.  (They are initted to; zero.;;   ctlNext;   ctlOwner;   ctlRect *****;   ctlFlag;   ctlHilite;   ----- ctlValue;   ctlProc;   ----- ctlAction;   ----- ctldata;   ctlRefCon;   ----- ctlColor *****;   ctlID;   ctlType;   ctlSize;   ctlMoreFlags;   defProcVerb;; ----- means needs setting; ***** means needs expanding;;====================================================================simp_init	proc EXPORT;-----------------------------------------------------------;; See who called us and init the fields accordingly.; (Use the high bit of the proc pointer to tell us.;	ldy #NewCtlRecord.CtlProc+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	bmi CalledByNewCtl2	brl CalledByNewCtlCalledByNewCtl2	phx	; save x;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Copy the TitleRef from the template to the control record; 3 out of 4 times, this is all there is to do.;	ldy #simpleButtonTemplate.TitleRef	lda [param],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [param],y	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlData+2	sta [ctlPtr],y	dey	dey	txa	sta [ctlPtr],y;-----------------------------------------------------------;; The title is now correct.  Lets move on to the optional; parameters.  First, we look at the pCount to see if ; there are any optionals.;; The number is different for simplebuttons and others.;	ldy #simpleButtonTemplate.ProcRef+3	lda [param],y	and #$007F	bne @NotSimple;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Its a simple button.  If the pcount is < 8, there are; no optional parameters.  If it is 8 there is only a ; color table.  If it is 9, there is a color table and; key equivalents.;@Simple	lda [param]	cmp #8	bcc NoCT	cmp #9	bcc YesCT	; no key equiv	ldy #SimpleButtonTemplate.KeyMods;; Store away the key equiv data.  Start with the ctlKeyMods;@JoinKeyEquiv	lda [param],y		; read the mods	tyx		; save y into x	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlKeyMods	; store away the mods	sta [ctlPtr],y	txy		; get y back from x	iny		; bump twice for care bits	iny	lda [param],y		; read care bits	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlKeyModsCareBits	; write into control record	sta [ctlPtr],y	txy		; get y back from x again	dey		; dec twice	dey	lda [param],y		; read in key1 and key2	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlKey1	; put into control record.	sta [ctlPtr],y	bra YesCT;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Its a radio or check box.  If the pcount is < 9, there are; no optional parameters.  If it is 9 there is only a ; color table.  If it is 10, there is a color table and; key equivalents.;@NotSimple	lda [param]	cmp #9	bcc NoCT	ldy #RadioTemplate.KeyMods	bra @JoinKeyEquiv;;;-----------------------------------------------------------;; There is a colortable ref.  The first thing we do is copy; it to the control record (just in case it is right). If ; we are using an offset, then we'll have to modify it below.;YesCT	jsr GetColorTableRefFromTemplate	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlColor	sta [ctlPtr],y	iny	iny	txa	sta [ctlPtr],yNoCT;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Now we have to set the value for radio and check controls;	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+3	lda [ctlPtr],y	and #$007F	beq NoValue	ldy #checkTemplate.value	lda [param],y	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlValue	sta [ctlPtr],yNoValue	plx	; restore x-regCalledByNewCtl;; --- Set default sizes if needed --------------------------------;	ldy #CtlRect+y2	Has the RECT already been set?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bne init_clr;	phx	Save control type.;	jsr pushfontInfo	Get text font information.	_GetFontInfo;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	pha	Space for width result.	jsr PushStringPtr	_StringWidth;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	pla	ldy #CtlRect+x1	Add width of title to starting position.	clc	adc [<Ctlptr],y;;	plx	Restore control type,	phx	and put back.	bmi do_simple	Is this a simple button.;;; --- Finish initializing check boxes and radio buttons ---------------;	pha	Save width so far.;	jsr get_csize	Get width and height of icon.;	ldy #fontInfo+ascent	lda [<data],y	Use max height of icon or text.	clc	iny	iny	adc [<data],y	ldy #rect2+y2	cmp [<data],y	bcc ok1	sta [<data],y	Use height of text instead of icon.;ok1	pla	Restore width so far,	clc	ldy #rect2+x2	adc [<data],y	plus width of icon,	adc #TITLE_SPACE	plus space between icon and title,	tax	and put total width	in x.	ldy #rect2+y2	Get height of icon,	lda [<data],y	bra store1	and compute bottom side, set right side.;;; --- Finish initaializing simple button ------------------------------;do_simple	adc #30	Plus a little extra	for simple buttons.	tax	Save right side in x.;          ;; ------ Now set the bottom side -------------------------------------;	ldy #fontInfo+ascent	lda [<data],y	Get system font's height.	clc	iny	iny	adc [<data],y	clc	adc #6	Add some leading.;store1	ldy #CtlRect+y1	clc	adc [<Ctlptr],y	Add the height to the top side.;	ldy #CtlRect+y2	sta [<Ctlptr],y	Store the bottom side.	iny	iny	txa	sta [<Ctlptr],y	Store the right side.;	plx;;; --- Set default color table if needed	--------------------------;;          x = $FFFF for simple button color table.;              else	check box color table.;init_clr	ldy #CtlColor+2	Color table pointer	already there?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bne exit	dey	dey	lda [<CtlPtr],y	bne exit;	iny	Get Y back to CtlColor+1	lda #butt_color>>8	sta [<Ctlptr],y	dey	lda #butt_color	Simple button color	table.	inx	Are we initializing	a simple button?	beq store2	lda #check_color	Check box/Radio button color table.store2	sta [<Ctlptr],yexit	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Test if given point is;          inside the enclosing RECT.;;   IN:    param = point to check, param = y, param+2 = x.;;  OUT:    a = part	code of found part,;              zero	if point not in enclosing RECT.;;====================================================================test_butt	proc EXPORT	lda #BUTT_PART	Simple button part code.		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Draw a simple button.;;   IN:    <ctlptr = control pointer.;          <rect = enclosing rectangle.;          <param =	part to draw.;          <colorptr = pointer to color	table to use.;;====================================================================simp_draw	proc EXPORTFrameRect	equ 4+256*83FillRect	equ 4+256*87FrameRRect	equ 4+256*93FillRRect	equ 4+256*97;;	jsr SetupColor	; colorPtr now valid	jsr CheckForVis	If not visible, don't come back	ldy #CtlFlag	Read the flag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	Save flag.	and #$0001	Bold/Single and drop shadow bit.	sta <work	txa;	ldx #FrameRect	Square corner functions.	ldy #FillRect;	and #$0002	Round or square corners.	sta <work+2	0=round, 2=square.	bne store1;	ldx #FrameRRect	Round corner functions.	ldy #FillRRect;store1	stx <work+4	Frame function.	sty <work+6	Fill function.;;; --- Draw round button's interior background and frame ------------;	jsr pushVvert_pen	pla	inc a	A little more for vertical lines.	pha	pea 1	_SetPenSize;	jsr pushrect	Pass pointer to RECT.;	lda <work+2	Round or square?	bne skip5;	ldx #13	ldy #GraphicsMode	lda [<data],y	320 or 640?	beq store2	ldx #26store2	phx	Oval width.	pea 8	Oval height for fill.;skip5	ldy #state	lda [<data],y	inc a	inc a	tay	jsr pushcolor	Pass pointer to color pattern.	ldx <work+6	Use Fill function.	jsl $E10000;	ldy #simpOutline	jsr pushcolor	Pass pointer to color pattern.	_SetPenPat	Set color of frame.;	jsr pushrect	Pass pointer to RECT.;	lda <work+2	Round or Square?	bne skip7;	ldx #13	ldy #GraphicsMode	lda [<data],y	320 or 640?	beq store3	ldx #26store3	phx	Oval width.	pea 8	Oval height for fill.;skip7	ldx <work+4	Frame function.	jsl $E10000;;; --- Draw special outlines ---------------------------------------------;	lda <work	Anything special?	beq skip1;	lda <work+2	Round or square?	beq roundBold;; ------ Drop shadow the square button ----------------------------------;	ldy <rect+x2	phy	Pass last point.	lda <rect+y1	inc a	inc a	pha;	phy	Set second point.	ldx <rect+y2	phx;	phx	Save x.	jsr pushVvert_pen	pla	Get vertical height	of lines.	plx	Restore x.	asl a	Set starting point.	clc	adc <rect+x1	pha	phx	_MoveTo	_LineTo	Bottom dropshadow.;	jsr pushVvert_pen	pla	asl a	Vertical width.	pha	Line width.	pea 1	Line height.	_SetPenSize	_LineTo;	bra skip1;;; ------ Draw a bold outline --------------------------------------------;roundBold	jsr expandButt;	jsr pushrect	Pass pointer to RECT.	ldx #18	ldy #GraphicsMode	lda [<data],y	320 or 640?	beq store4	ldx #36store4	phx	Oval width.	pea 12	Oval height.	_FrameRRect;	jsr CMsetrect	Restore enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;skip1	_PenNormal;;; --- Print string in button ----------------------;; ------ Find title's width -----------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	pha	Space to width result.	jsr PushStringPtr	_StringWidth;;; ------ Center title horizontally ----------------;	lda <rect+x2	sec	sbc <rect+x1	Width of button.	sbc 1,s	Less width of string.	lsr a	Half way.	clc	adc <rect+x1	Starting position.	tax	Pass X starting position in x.	pla	Get rid of width.;	brl drawtitle	Print title in button.;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = =;          Expand button for bold outine.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = =;;   IN:    rect = RECT to expand, and is equal to button's enclosing RECT.;;  OUT:    rect = size of bolded button.;	EXPORT expandButtexpandButt		;       ;	jsr pushrect	Pass pointer of RECT to expand.;	jsr pushVvert_pen	pla	inc a	eor #$FFFF	Make it expand.;          inc   a	pha	pea $FFFE	_InsetRect		rts;	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Invals bounding rect of control;;   IN:    ctlPtr;;  OUT:    a and x = 0;;====================================================================Inval_rect	proc	lda ctlPtr	clc	adc #NewCtlRecord.ctlRect	tax	lda ctlPtr+2	adc #0	pha	phx	_InvalRect	tax		rts		ENDP		title 'CHECK_PROC';====================================================================;;          Main line Check Box handler.;;   IN:    a = task.;          Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          param = additional parameter.;;  OUT:    a = low word of returned value.;          x = high	word of returned value.;;====================================================================check_proc 	proc EXPORT	cmp #ctlWinStateChange+1	make sure I can handle message	bcc @ok	brl null_ret@ok	asl a	Compute index for dispatch.	tax	lda >task_list,x	pha	ldx #0	Check box number.	rts	Complete the task.;task_list	DC.W check_draw-1	Draw.	DC.W null_ret-1	Compute drag RECT.	DC.W checkboxHit-1	Hit test routine.	DC.W simp_init-1	Initialize the control.	DC.W simp_disp-1	Dispose.	DC.W check_draw-1	New value.	DC.W null_ret-1	Compute Thumber constrains.	DC.W null_ret-1	Drag the indicator.	DC.W null_ret-1	Auto action.	DC.W check_draw-1	New value.	DC.W null_ret-1	Set min max.	DC.W null_ret-1	Move control.	DC.W nor_size-1	Return size of standard record.	dc.W nor_event-1	13 Handle events	dc.W null_ret-1	14 ctlChangeTarget	dc.W null_ret-1	15 ctlChagneBounds	dc.W null_ret-1	16 ctlWindChagneSize	dc.W null_ret-1	17 ctlHandleTab	dc.W null_ret-1	18 ctlNotifyMultiPart	dc.W Inval_rect-1	19 ctlWinStateChange (just inval)	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Test if given point is;          inside the enclosing RECT.;;   IN:    param = point to check, param = y, param+2 = x.;;  OUT:    a = check box part code of found part.;;  To get this far,	the point must be inside the control's enclosing RECT.;  So, just return the part code to signal a hit.;;====================================================================checkboxHit	proc EXPORT	lda #CHECK_PART	Return part code in	A.		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Draw a check box.;;   IN:    rect = control's enclosing rectangle.;          state = 0 if unhilited, 2 if	hilited.;          active =	0 if active, $FFFF if inactive.;;;====================================================================check_draw	proc EXPORT	ldx #0	Check box icon number.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = =;          Draw radio button or check box.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = =;;   IN:    x = 0 for check box, 4 for radio button.;          <rect = control's enclosing rectangle.;          <colorptr = pointer to color	table to use.;          state = 0 if unhilited, 2 if	hilited.;          active =	0 if active, $FFFF if inactive.;	EXPORT radio_checkradio_check		;       	jsr CheckForVis	If not visible, don't come back--x preserved		phx	Save the icon number since it might get trashed by 	jsr SetupColor	SetupColor if we need to load a resource.;; --- Draw icon -----------------------------------------------;	plx	Restore the icon number.	phx	Get icon number in x, but save number on stack still	ldy #CtlValue	Is the box checked?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	beq skip1	inx	inxskip1	jsr print_icon	Draw the icon.		plx	Restore icon number in x as input for get_csize	lda <param	Does the title need	to be drawn?	beq ok1	Only if drawing whole control.		rtsok1	jsr get_csize	Get the size of the	icon. ;	ldy #rect2+x2	Width of the icon,	lda [<data],y	clc	adc <rect+x1	plus starting x position,	adc #TITLE_SPACE	plus space,	tax	equals title's starting x position.;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =;        Draw control's title.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =;;   IN:  state = 0 for normal, 2 for hilited.;        x = starting x position of text.;        <rect = control's enclosing rectangle.;;  OUT:  Title centered vertically and printed.;	EXPORT DrawTitledrawtitle		;       	phx	Save.	jsr pushfontInfo	Get text font information.	_GetFontInfo	plx	Restore.;	lda <rect+y2	Center text vertically in 'rect'.	sec	sbc <rect+y1	Height of button.	ldy #fontInfo+ascent	sbc [<data],y	Less height of string.	bcc ck_dimm	Does the title fit?	lsr a	Half way.	clc	adc <rect+y1	Starting position.	clc	adc [<data],y	tay	Pass starting Y position.	jsr set_penpos	Set pen position.;;	pha	Space for result.	_GetFontFlags	pha	Space for result.	_GetTextMode;;	lda #SimpNorText	jsr set_textmode;	pea 4	Use word of color.	_SetFontFlags;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	jsr PushStringPtr	_DrawString	Print string.;	_SetTextMode	Restore original text mode.	_SetFontFlags	Restore original text flags.;;	EXPORT ck_dimmck_dimm		;       ;	ldy #active	Is the control active?	lda [<data],y	bpl exit	If yes, don't disable.;;; --- Disable the control -----------------------------------------;	pea dimmed>>16	Set pen to dim mask.	pea dimmed	_SetPenMask;		jsr pushrect	Pass pointer of item's RECT.;	                  	Disabled can't be selected.;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #Ctlproc+2	Is the control a simple button?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$7FFF	Make sure we mask off the high bit just in case this is super	bne ItsSquare	ldy #Ctlflag	Its a simple button, but is it square or round	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$0002		bne ItsSquare	Button is square;	pea 12	oval width (defining rounded corner of button)	pea 12	oval height;	inc <rect+y1	Inset the control's rect	dec <rect+y2	Don't disable outline of simple button	jsr pushVvert_pen	(only reason to do this is because the MAC does this)	lda <rect+x1	clc	adc 1,s	sta <rect+x1	lda <rect+x2	sec 	sbc 1,s	sta <rect+x2	pla	Get vertical pen width off stack		ldy #simpNorText	jsr pushcolor	Push pointer to color pattern.	_FillRRect	FillRect function number	bra skip4;;ItsSquare	ldy #simpNorText	jsr pushcolor	Push pointer to color pattern.	_FillRect	FillRect function number;skip4	pea nor_mask>>16	Reset drawing mask to normal solid.	pea nor_mask	_SetPenMask;exit	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Print an	icon.;;   IN:    x = icon	number.;          state = hilite state.;          rect = where to print.;;====================================================================print_icon	proc EXPORT	ldy #state	lda [<data],y	beq ok1	txa	ora #1	Use hilited version	of icon.	tax;ok1	txa;;	EXPORT draw_icondraw_icon		;       	sta <work	Store icon (character) number.	jsr get_csize2	Get icon's size.;           	lda <rect+y2	Center icon vertically in 'rect'.	sec	sbc <rect+y1	Height of button.	ldy #rect2+y2*** added 21-Apr-91 DAL -- draws icon in correct location if top coord is negative	sec*** end of 21-Apr-91 DAL	sbc [<data],y	Less height of icon.	bcc dontFit	lsr a	Half way.	clc	adc <rect+y1	Starting position.	tay	Pass starting Y position.	ldx <rect+x1	jsr set_penpos	Set pen position.;	pha	Space for result.	_GetFontFlags	Save state.	pha	Space for result.	_GetTextMode	Save state.;	lda #simpNorBack	Icon color index.	jsr set_textmode	Set icon color and OR mode.;	lda #drawChar	Address of function	to perform while	jsr doIconFunc	icon font is current.;	_SetTextMode	Restore original text mode.	_SetFontFlags	Restore original text flags.		rtsdrawChar	pei <work	Pass character (icon number) to print.	_DrawChar	dontFit	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;        Move pen to a given point without drawing.;;   IN:    y = y coordinate.;          x = x coordinate.;;====================================================================set_penpos	proc EXPORT	phx	phy	_MoveTo		rts		ENDP	title 'RADIO_PROC';====================================================================;;          Main line Radio Button handler.;;   IN:    a = task.;          Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          param = additional parameter.;;  OUT:    a = low word of returned value.;          x = high	word of returned value.;;====================================================================radio_proc 	proc EXPORT	cmp #ctlWinStateChange+1	make sure I can handle message	bcc @ok	brl null_ret@ok	asl a	Compute index for dispatch.	tax	lda >task_list,x	pha	ldx #4	Radio button number.	rts	Complete the task.;task_list	DC.W radio_draw-1	Draw.	DC.W null_ret-1	Compute drag RECT.	DC.W radioHit-1	Common hit test routine.	DC.W simp_init-1	Initialize the control.	DC.W simp_disp-1	Dispose.	DC.W radio_draw-1	Called after drag.	DC.W null_ret-1	Compute Thumber constrains.	DC.W null_ret-1	Drag the indicator.	DC.W null_ret-1	Auto action.	DC.W radio_set-1	New value.	DC.W null_ret-1	Set min max.	DC.W null_ret-1	Move control.	DC.W nor_size-1	Return size of standard record.	dc.W nor_event-1	13 Handle events	dc.W null_ret-1	14 ctlChangeTarget	dc.W null_ret-1	15 ctlChagneBounds	dc.W null_ret-1	16 ctlWindChagneSize	dc.W null_ret-1	17 ctlHandleTab	dc.W null_ret-1	18 ctlNotifyMultiPart	dc.W Inval_rect-1	19 ctlWinStateChange (just inval)	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Test if given point is;          inside the enclosing RECT.;;   IN:    param = point to check, param = y, param+2 = x.;;  OUT:    a = check box part code of found part.;;  To get this far,	the point must be inside the control's enclosing RECT.;  So, just return the part code to signal a hit.;;====================================================================radioHit	proc EXPORT	lda #RADIO_PART	Return part code in	A.		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Draw a radio button.;;====================================================================radio_draw	proc EXPORT	ldx #4	Radio button icon number.	brl radio_check	Draw radio button.		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Set a new value for a radio button.;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          windptr = pointer of control's window.;;  OUT:    None.;;====================================================================radio_set	proc EXPORTfamilyNum	equ worktempCtl	equ familyNum+2;;	jsr radio_draw	Draw the button in its new state.;;; --- Make sure two	buttons in the same	family are not on -------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlValue	Is button being turned off?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	(Set return flag.)	beq exit	If yes, I don't have to worry about;	                  	other radio buttons in this family.;;; --- Check if there are any buttons in	this family on ---------------;	lda <Ctlhand	Save handle of this	control.	sta <tempCtl	lda <Ctlhand+2	sta <tempCtl+2;	ldy #CtlFlag	Get this radio button's family number.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$007F	sta <familyNum;	ldy #owControls	Get head of control	list.	lda [<windptr],y	sta <Ctlhand	iny	lda [<windptr],y	sta <Ctlhand+1	(And I know there must be at least;	                   	one control in the control list. );	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;;lop1	jsr next_radio	beq exit	Is no other radio button set?;	lda <Ctlhand	Check if I found the one just set.	cmp <tempCtl	bne gotit	lda <Ctlhand+1	cmp <tempCtl+1	bne gotit	If not, I've found a family member on.;	jsr next_Ctl	If yes, skip it, and start from there.	bne lop1	End of the line?		rtsgotit	ldy #CtlValue	Turn the other radio button off.	lda #0	sta [<Ctlptr],y;	ldy #CtlFlag	Redraw the radio button if visible.	lda [<ctlptr],y	and #CTL_INVIS	bne exit;	ldy #state	Unhilte.	lda #0	sta [<data],y	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.	jsr radio_draw	Draw the button turned off.;exit	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Find the	next on radio button in a family.;;   IN:    Ctlhand = handle of Ctlptr.;          work = family number.;;  OUT:    Ctlptr =	next on radio button in family, zero if	none found.;          Ctlhand = handle of Ctlptr.;          Equal flag is TRUE if no control found.;          Equal flag is FALSE if control found.;;====================================================================next_radio	proc EXPORT	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).lop1	ldy #Ctlproc 	Is the control a radio button?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bne next1	iny	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$7FFF	; ignore super control bit	cmp #$0400	bne next1;	ldy #CtlFlag	Check for matching family number.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$007F	cmp <work	bne next1;	ldy #CtlValue	Is it on?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bne exit	If yes, I've found it.;next1	jsr next_Ctl	Next control.	bne lop1;exit	rts	ENDP	title 'GROW_PROC';====================================================================;;          Grow box	definition proc EXPORTedure.;;   IN:    a = task.;          Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          param = additional parameter.;;  OUT:    a = low word of returned value.;          x = high	word of returned value.;;====================================================================grow_proc 	proc EXPORT	cmp #ctlWinStateChange+1	bcc @1	brl null_ret@1	asl a	Compute index for dispatch.	tax	jmp (grow_tasks,x)grow_tasks	DC.W draw_grow	0  Draw grow box.	DC.W null_ret	1  Compute drag RECT.	DC.W test_grow	2  Common hit test routine.	DC.W init_grow	3  Initialize just the color table.	DC.W null_ret	4  Dispose.	DC.W draw_grow	5  New value.	DC.W null_ret	6  Compute Thumber constrains.	DC.W track_grow	7  Drag the indicator.	DC.W null_ret	8  Auto action.	DC.W draw_grow	9  New value.	DC.W null_ret	10 Set min max.	DC.W null_ret	11 Move button.	DC.W nor_size	12 Return size of standard record.	dc.W null_ret	13 ctlHandleEvent	dc.W null_ret	14 ctlChangeTarget	dc.W null_ret	15 ctlChagneBounds	dc.W null_ret	16 ctlWindChagneSize	dc.W null_ret	17 ctlHandleTab	dc.W null_ret	18 ctlNotifyMultiPart	dc.W Inval_rect	19 ctlWinStateChange (just inval)	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Draw a grow box.;;   IN:    <param =	0 to draw entire control, state = 0.;	part code to draw just that part of the	control.;;           state =	0 to draw part in 'param' as unhighlighted.;	2 to draw part in 'param' as highlighted.;;           active = $0000 if control is active.;	 $FFFF if control is inactive, param = 0.;;====================================================================draw_grow	proc EXPORT	jsr CheckForVis	If not visible, don't come back	jsr SetupColor	ldy #state	lda [<data],y	clc	adc #simpNorBack	tay	lda [<colorPtr],y	and #$00F0	tay	Pass color of interior.	lda [<colorPtr]	Pass color of frame.	and #$00F0	jsr drawRect	Draw outline and interior.;;	ldy #active	Is control inactive?	lda [<data],y	bmi exit	If inactive, don't draw icon.;	ldx #GROW_ICON	jsr get_csize	Get the size of the	grow icon.;	jsr center_hor	Center grow box horizontally.	bcc exit	Does the icon fix inside the RECT?;	lda #GROW_ICON	brl draw_icon;exit	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Initialize grow box record.;;====================================================================test_grow	proc EXPORT	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlFlag	lda [ctlPtr],y	and #$0001	beq NeverMind	lda #$80	; return a value that will force	rts	; us to do the tracking.NeverMind	lda #GROW_PART	Must be hit to get this far.		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;; track the grow box by calling the window manager;;====================================================================track_grow	proc	lda param	tax	beq DoNothing	pha	; save the current origin	pha	pha	pha	tsc	inc a	pea 0000	pha	_GetPortRect	lda #0	; set origin to zero (only works with zero origin)	pha	pha	_SetOrigin;; See if any minimum size is in ctlData field.  zero means use default.;	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlData	lda [ctlPtr],y	bne @1	lda #50	; minimum y@1	tax	iny	iny	lda [ctlPtr],y	bne @2	lda #130	; minimum x@2		pha	; space for result	pha	pha	; use (30,10) more in each direction, so we end up being the	phx	;..same as task master.	pha	; read the mouse in global coordinates	pha	pha	_ReadMouse	pla	; ignore the mode word, leave x and y on stack.	jsr PushWindowPtr	_GrowWindow	jsr PushWindowPtr	_SizeWindow	_SetOrigin	; restore origin to top left of original port rect	pla	; remove bottom right from stack	pla	lda param	; return the part code to indicate that	tax	; that we handled the work.  X indicates not aborted.DoNothing	rts	PushWindowPtr	plx	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlOwner+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [ctlPtr],y	pha	phx	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Init the Grow Control;; Change History;; 10 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; Added code to make this work with NewControl2.;;====================================================================init_grow	proc EXPORT	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	bpl OldWay	;-----------------------------------------------------------;; This is being called from NewControl2.  This means that; Param holds pointer to the template.  CtlColor is not set; up.;; We fiddle with the data as follows:;    Check the pcount to see if there is a color table;    If YES, copy ref to CtlColor;    Fall into old code.;	ldy #GrowTemplate.pcount	lda [param],y	cmp #7	bne NoColorTable	ldy #GrowTemplate.ColorRef	lda [param],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [param],y	ldy #NewCtlRecord.CtlColor+2	sta [ctlPtr],y	dey	dey	txa	sta [ctlPtr],yNoColorTableOldWay	ldy #CtlColor+2	Color table pointer	already there?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	dey	dey	ora [<Ctlptr],y	bne exit;	lda #grow_color	sta [<Ctlptr],y	y-reg still set to #CtlColor	iny	iny	lda #^grow_color	sta [<Ctlptr],y;exit	rts	ENDP	title 'SCROLL_PROC';====================================================================;;          Main line Scroll Bar handler.;;   IN:    a = task.;          Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          param = additional parameter.;;  OUT:    a = low word of returned value.;          x = high	word of returned value.;;====================================================================scroll_proc 	proc EXPORT	cmp #ctlWinStateChange+1	bcc @1	brl null_ret@1	asl a	Compute index for dispatch.	tax	jmp (scroll_task_list,x) Complete the task.;;	export scroll_task_listscroll_task_list	DC.W scroll_draw	0 Draw.	DC.W null_ret	1 Compute drag RECT.	DC.W scroll_hit	2 Common hit test routine.	DC.W scroll_init	3 Initialize the control.	DC.W null_ret	4 Dispose.	DC.W null_ret	5 Called after drag	is completed.	DC.W null_ret	6 Setup for dragging.	DC.W null_ret	7 Perform dragging.	DC.W null_ret	8 Auto track.	DC.W move_thumb	9 New value.	DC.W newView	10 Called with new Min and Max values.	DC.W move_bar	11 Move scroll bar.	DC.W rec_size	12 Return size of scroll bar record.	dc.W null_ret	13 ctlhandleEvent	dc.W null_ret	14 ctlChangeTarget	dc.W null_ret	15 ctlChagneBounds	dc.W null_ret	16 ctlWindChagneSize	dc.W null_ret	17 ctlHandleTab	dc.W null_ret	18 ctlNotifyMultiPart	dc.W Inval_rect	19 ctlWinStateChange (just inval)	ENDP	title 'SCROLL_PROC -- rec_size';====================================================================;;          Return size of required record.;;====================================================================rec_size	proc EXPORT	lda param	ora param+2	beq OldSize	lda #SuperCtlSize	bra ReturnItOldSize	lda #PageRegion+8	Size of scroll bar record.ReturnIt	ldx #0	High word of size.		rts		ENDP	title 'SCROLL_PROC -- scroll_init';====================================================================;;          Initialize scroll bar.;; Change History;; 24 Jul 88	Steven Glass;; Added control value validation.;;; 10 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; Added code to translate NewCtl2 inputs to NewCtl inputs.;; 07 Dec 88	STeven Glass & Mensch;; Fixed bug with color table ref's and control templates.  The; code bne'd when it should have beq'd for pCount of 9.;;====================================================================scroll_init	proc EXPORT*** added 9-Jan-92 DAL -- set valid port	pha	pha	_GetPort	pha	pha	_GetWMgrPort	_SetPort*** end 9-Jan-92*** added 9-Dec-91 DAL -- check for new color table	_CtlNewRes*** end 9-Dec-91	_SetPort	;9-Jan-92 DAL	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	bpl OldWay	;-----------------------------------------------------------;; This is being called from NewControl2.  This means that; Param holds pointer to the template.  CtlColor is not set; up.  DataSize and ViewSize are not in Param.;; We fiddle with the data as follows:;    Copy the intital thumb value from template to record.;    Check the pcount to see if there is a color table;    If YES, copy ref to CtlColor;    Copy DataSize and ViewSize to Param;    Fall into old code.;	ldy #ScrollTemplate.InitialThumb	lda [param],y	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlValue	sta [ctlPtr],y	ldy #ScrollTemplate.pcount	is there a color table	lda [param],y	cmp #9	beq NoColorTable	ldy #ScrollTemplate.ColorRef	yes, put its ref in.	lda [param],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [param],y	ldy #NewCtlRecord.CtlColor+2	sta [ctlPtr],y	dey	dey	txa	sta [ctlPtr],yNoColorTable			;finished with color table	ldy #ScrollTemplate.DataSize	;fix param and fall into old way	lda [param],y	tax	ldy #ScrollTemplate.ViewSize	lda [param],y	sta param	stx param+2OldWay;; --- Validate the maximum value ------;	lda param+2	; Max allowable value is Max-View	sec	sbc param	ldy #Ctlvalue	; compare to the current value	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	; from control record	bcs @MaxOK	; ok	lda [<Ctlptr],y	; Bump max so it is equal to value+view	clc	adc <param	sta <param+2	; adjust the max value.@MaxOK	cmp <param	; is it greater than the min value?;; --- Set view and data size -----------------------;	ldy #Ctldata	lda <param	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <param+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Set default color table pointer --------------;	ldy #CtlColor+1	lda [<Ctlptr],y	dey	ora [<Ctlptr],y	bne skip1;	lda #scroll_color	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda #scroll_color>>16	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Set sizes --------------------------------------------;skip1	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;	ldx #uArrowH	Use up arrow for vertical bar,	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #DIR_SCROLL	beq ok1	ldx #lArrowH	and left arrow for horizontal bars.ok1	txy	lda [<data],y	Height of arrow icon,	clc	adc #3	plus leading,	ldy #rect2+y2	sta [<data],y	equals total size.;	txy	iny	Width of arrow icon,	iny	lda [<data],y	clc	adc #8	plus leading,	ldy #rect2+x2	sta [<data],y	equals total size.;;; ------ Set default height --------------------------------------;	lda <rect+y2	Is it set?	bne skip2;	lda <rect+y1	clc	ldy #rect2+y2	adc [<data],y	sta <rect+y2	ldy #CtlRect+y2	sta [<Ctlptr],y	Set height of enclosing RECT.;skip2	lda <rect+x2	Is it set?	bne skip3;	lda <rect+x1	clc	ldy #rect2+x2	adc [<data],y	sta <rect+x2	ldy #CtlRect+x2	sta [<Ctlptr],y	Set width of enclosing RECT.;;; ------ Set page region, by subtracting arrows from enclosing RECT ------;skip3	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	pha	and #UP_FLAG	beq skip10;	lda <rect+y1	clc	ldy #rect2+y2	Add height of icon plus leading.	adc [<data],y	sta <rect+y1;skip10	lda 1,s	and #DOWN_FLAG	beq skip11;	lda <rect+y2	sec	ldy #rect2+y2	sbc [<data],y	sta <rect+y2;skip11	lda 1,s	and #LEFT_FLAG	beq skip12;	lda <rect+x1	clc	ldy #rect2+x2	adc [<data],y	sta <rect+x1;skip12	pla	and #RIGHT_FLAG	beq skip13;	lda <rect+x2	sec	ldy #rect2+x2	sbc [<data],y	sta <rect+x2;skip13	ldy #PageRegion+x2	Initialize page region.	jsr to_Ctl	Move 'rect' into page region.;	jsr pushrect	Indent thumber from	page region.	jsr pushVvert_pen	pea 1	_InsetRect;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #Thumb+x2	jsr to_Ctl	Move 'rect' into thumber RECT.;;; --- Set thumber position ---------------------------;	brl new_thumb;====================================================================;;          Move 'rect' into control RECT.;;  IN:     y = offset into record plus x2.;;====================================================================to_Ctl		ldx #x2lop1	lda <rect,x	sta [<Ctlptr],y	dey	Anything for some bytes.	dex	bpl lop1	rts		ENDP	title 'SCROLL_PROC -- scroll_hit';====================================================================;;          Check hit on scroll bar.;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	pointer to scroll bar record.;          param = y coordinate to check.;          param+2 = x coordinate to check.;;  OUT:    a = 0 if	no hit.;              5 if	on up arrow.;              6 if	on down arrow.;              7 if	on page up region.;              8 if	on page down region.;            129 if	on thumber.;;====================================================================scroll_hit	proc EXPORT	ldy #CtlData	lda [<Ctlptr],y	Total view.	iny	iny	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	Total data area.	bcc ok1;	lda #0	No hit anywhere if maxed out.		rtsok1	ldy #PageRegion	Check page region.	jsr check_pt	beq next1	ldy #Thumb	Check thumber.	jsr check_pt	ldx #THUMB_PART	Part code, just in case.	tay	Was it a hit?	bne got_it;; --- Must be in page region, up or down? -----------------;	ldx #UPP_PART	Page up part code.	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #DIR_SCROLL	Vertical or horizontal bar?	bne horizontal;	lda <param	Get y coordinate.	ldy #Thumb+y1	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	bcc got_it	inx	Page down part code.	bra got_it	Must be page down.;;horizontal	lda <param+2	Get x coordinate.	ldy #Thumb+x1	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	bcc got_it	inx	Page down part code.	bra got_it	Must be page down.;;; --- Must be in an	arrow box ------------------------------;next1	ldx #UP_PART;	ldy #PageRegion+y1	lda <param	Get y coordinate.	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	bcc got_it;	inx	Down arrow part code.;	ldy #PageRegion+y2	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	bcs got_it;	dex	Back to up arrow.;	ldy #PageRegion+x1	lda <param+2	Get x coordinate.	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	bcc got_it	inx	Down arrow part code.got_it	txa	rts;;;   IN:    y = offset into record to check + x2.;	EXPORT check_ptcheck_pt		;       ;	pha	Space for result.	lda #param	jsr pushzpage	Pass pointer of point to check.	tya	jsr pushrecord	Pass pointer of RECT to check.	_PtInRect	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	pla	rts;	ENDP	title 'SCROLL_PROC -- scroll_draw';====================================================================;;          Draw a scroll bar.;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	control pointer.;          param = part to draw.;;====================================================================scroll_draw	proc EXPORT	jsr CheckForVis	If not vis, don't come back.*** added 9-Dec-91 DAL -- if we're part of an extended list, force focus frame update	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlFlag	lda [<ctlPtr],y	and #$0040	;partOfExtendedList	beq @notExtended*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- Preserve State around this CallCtlDefProc	ldy #state	lda [<data],y	pha*** end 6-Feb-92	pha	pha	;space for CallCtlDefProc result	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlRefCon+2	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<ctlPtr],y	pha	;push List handle (from scroll refcon)	pea ctlChangeActivity	pea 0	pea 0	;reserved	_CallCtlDefProc	pla	pla	;discard result*** added 6-Feb-92 DAL -- Restore State so arrows will hilite properly	pla	ldy #state	sta [<data],y*** end 6-Feb-92@notExtended*** end 9-Dec-91 DAL	jsr SetupColor	lda <param	Get part code.	and #$7F	asl a	tax	jmp (part_list,x);;part_list	DC.W draw_all	0 Draw entire control.	DC.W draw_thumb	1 Draw thumber.	DC.W 0	2	DC.W 0	3	DC.W 0	4	DC.W draw_up1	5 Draw up arrow.	DC.W draw_down1	6 Draw down arrow.	DC.W null_ret	7 Draw page region.	DC.W null_ret	8 Draw page region.;;;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;          Draw entire scroll bar.;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;draw_all	ldy #active	lda [<data],y	Is control inactive?	bpl skip100;; --- Draw an inactive scroll bar --------------------------;	ldy #InactiveColor	Inactive color.	lda [<colorPtr],y	and #$00F0	tay	Pass interior color.	lda [<colorPtr]	Pass frame color.	and #$00F0	brl drawrect	Draw and exit.;;; --- Draw an active scroll bar -----------------------------;skip100	jsr inner_scroll	Draw interior of scroll bar.;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	pha	and #UP_FLAG	Up arrow?	beq next100;	jsr draw_up2	Draw up arrow.;next100	lda 1,s	and #DOWN_FLAG	Down arrow?	beq next101;	jsr draw_down2	Draw down arrow.;next101	lda 1,s	and #LEFT_FLAG	Left arrow?	beq next102;	jsr draw_left2	Draw left arrow.;next102	pla	and #RIGHT_FLAG	Right arrow?	beq exit100;	    	brl draw_right2	Draw right arrow.;exit100	rts;;	EXPORT inner_scrollinner_scroll		;       ;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlData	lda [<Ctlptr],y	Total view.	iny	iny	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	Total data area.	bcc ok100	Everything in view?;	ldy #active	Set active flag for	arrows.	lda #$FFFF	sta [<data],y;	ldy #ThumbNorColor	Use thumber's color to draw page region.	brl draw_page;ok100	ldy #PageRgnColor	Page region's color and pattern.	jsr draw_page	Draw page region.;	brl draw_thumb	Draw thumber.;;;;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;          Draw up arrow.;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;draw_up1	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlFlag	Vertical or horizontal?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #DIR_SCROLL	bne draw_left2;draw_up2	jsr up_box	Draw up arrow box.;	ldx #UP_ARROW	Up arrow pattern index.	brl draw_arrow2;;;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;          Draw down arrow.;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;draw_down1	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlFlag	Vertical or horizontal?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #DIR_SCROLL	bne draw_right2;draw_down2	jsr down_box	Draw down arrow box.;	ldx #DOWN_ARROW	Down arrow pattern index.	brl draw_arrow2;;            ;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;          Draw left arrow.  ;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;	                  draw_left2	jsr left_box	Draw left arrow box.;	ldx #LEFT_ARROW	Left arrow pattern index.	brl draw_arrow2;;            ;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;          Draw right arrow.;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;draw_right2	jsr right_box	Draw right arrow box.;	ldx #RITE_ARROW	Right arrow pattern	index.	brl draw_arrow2;;;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;          Draw page region.;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;         draw_page	phy	Save color to use.;	lda [<colorptr]	Get outline color.	tay	jsr set_patt	phx	phy	_SetPenPat;	ldy #PageRegion+x2	jsr CMsetrect2	Set 'rect' to page region.	ply;	jsr pushrect	For FillRect call.	phy	Pass color.;	jsr pushrect	Pass address of RECT to frame.	_FrameRect;;	jsr pushrect	jsr pushVvert_pen	pea 1	_InsetRect;	ply	Color index to use.	lda [<colorptr],y	tay	jsr set_patt	phx	phy	_FillRect;	brl dereference;;;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;          Draw scroll bar thumb.;= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =;	EXPORT draw_thumbdraw_thumb		;       ;	ldy #Thumb+x2	jsr CMsetrect2	Put thumber coordinates into 'rect'.;	ldy #ThumbNorColor	Index to color of thumb.	lda [<colorPtr],y	and #$00F0	tay	Pass interior color.	lda [<colorPtr]	Pass frame color.	and #$00F0	jsr drawrect;	brl dereference		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Draw a up arrow box.;;====================================================================up_box	proc EXPORT	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #PageRegion+y1	lda [<Ctlptr],y	inc a	sta <rect+y2	bra common;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;          Draw a down arrow box.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;	EXPORT down_boxdown_box		;       ;	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #PageRegion+y2	lda [<Ctlptr],y	dec a	sta <rect+y1	bra common;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;          Draw a left arrow box.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;	EXPORT left_boxleft_box		;       ;	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #PageRegion+x1	lda [<Ctlptr],y	inc a	sta <rect+x2	bra common;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;          Draw a right arrow box.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;	EXPORT right_boxright_box		;       ;	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #PageRegion+x2	lda [<Ctlptr],y	dec a	sta <rect+x1;common	lda #simpNorBack	Arrow box's interior color index.	clc	ldy #state	adc [<data],y	tay	lda [<colorPtr],y	and #$00F0	tay	Pass interior color.	lda [<colorPtr]	Pass frame color.	and #$00F0	jsr drawrect	Draw box.;	brl dereference		ENDP	title 'SCROLL_PROC -- utilities';====================================================================;;          Draw a scroll bar arrow.;;   IN:    state = 0 to draw normal, 2 to draw as selected.;          colorptr	= pointer to color table.;          rect = enclosing RECT.;          x = icon	number.;;  OUT:    rect = arrow's enclosing RECT.;;====================================================================draw_arrow2	proc EXPORT	phx;	lda >arrowMap-UP_ARROW,x	tay	lda [<data],y	Get height of arrow.	tyx	ldy #rect2+y2	sta [<data],y	txy	iny	iny	lda [<data],y	Get width of arrow.	ldy #rect2+x2	sta [<data],y;	plx	jsr center_hor	Center the arrow horizontally.	bcc exit	Did the arrow fit in the box?;;	                  x	= icon to print.	jsr print_icon	Print arrow icon.;	brl dereference;exit	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Center an icon horizontally.;;   IN:    rect2+x2	= icon's width.;          rect = RECT to center in.;;  OUT:    Carry flag is clear if icon won't fit inside of 'rect'.;          rect+x1 = starting position of icon to be horizontally center.;          x = unchanged.;;====================================================================center_hor	proc EXPORT	lda <rect+x2	Get width of box.	sec	sbc <rect+x1	sec	ldy #rect2+x2	Less width of arrow.	sbc [<data],y	bcc exit	Arrow won't fix in arrow box.	lsr a	Half way.	clc	adc <rect+x1	sta <rect+x1	X point to draw arrow.;	sec	Set OK flag.exit	rts	ENDP	     ;====================================================================;;        Set new Minimum and Maximum for scroll bar.;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	pointer to scroll bar.;          param = new view, $FFFF to not set.;          param+2 = new data size, $FFFF to not set.;; Change History;; 24 Jul 88	Steven Glass;; If the view was not changed but the maximum value was changed,; the code was not going through the validation that it goes through; when the view is changed.  This allowed the max to be less than; the view.;; Added new label @skip2 which is now branched to when view is not; changed.  old code branched straight to redraw.;; Note that this code already tried to maintain a valid value, but; could fail to do so under certain circumstances.;;====================================================================newView	proc EXPORToffset	equ work	Zero page usage.height	equ offset+2	Height of page region.front	equ height+2thumb_h	equ front+2	Height of thumber.trect	equ thumb_h+2	jsr  scrollState	php	jsr  dereference		;ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	ldy  #CtlData+2		;set the parameters to the new view and	lda  <param+2		;..data size for the scroll bar. The	cmp  #$FFFF		;..reason they weren't already is that	bne  @useParam2		;..one of them could be $FFFF (no change)	lda  [<ctlPtr],y@useParam2	sta  <param+2	dey	dey	lda  <param	cmp  #$FFFF	bne  @useParam	lda  [<ctlPtr],y@useParam	sta  <param	lda  <param+2	sec	sbc  <param	bcs  @1	lda  #0@1	ldy  #CtlValue		;is the new maximum less than the current	cmp  [<ctlPtr],y		;..value ? If not, then reset the value	bcs  @valueOK		;..to the maximum value.	sta  [<ctlPtr],y	bra  @setAndDraw@valueOK	ldy  #CtlData+2	lda  <param+2	cmp  [<ctlPtr],y	bne  @setAndDraw	dey	dey	lda  <param	cmp  [<ctlPtr],y	bne  @setAndDraw	plp		;nothing changed, so just exit	rts@setAndDraw	ldy  #CtlData+2	lda  <param+2	sta  [<ctlPtr],y	dey	dey	lda  <param	sta  [<ctlPtr],y	jsr  new_thumb	jsr scrollState	Is scroll bar drawable?	bcc ok2	plp	bcc noexit	rtsnoexit	phpok2	plp	jsr SetupColor	brl inner_scroll	Draw interior of scroll bar.;;;;====================================================================;;        Set new value for thumb;;   IN:    param has new value of thumb;          param+2 has old value of thumb;; Change History;; 24 Jul 88	Steven Glass;; When the thumb value is changed we validate the existing ; Max value.  If the thumb has a value that is greater than the; MaxValue - ViewSize then something is wrong so we adjust MaxValue.;; The new MaxValue is set to NewThumbValue+ViewSize.;; This prevents the thumb from drawing outside the scroll bar or on; the arrows.;;====================================================================lastScrollTime	dc.w 0	;added 4-Jan-91 DAL	EXPORT move_thumbmove_thumb;; 4-Jan-91 DAL;; Max out the scrolling speed to a fixed amount of time.; If it hasn't been minScrollDelay since the last time we; moved the thumb, wait until it has.;	pha	;space for result	lda >lastScrollTime	pha	pea MinScrollDelay	_WaitUntil	pla	sta >lastScrollTime;;--- Validate the new value -----------------------------------------;	ldy #Ctldata+2	; compute maximum allowable value	lda [<CtlPtr],y	; as Max-View	dey	dey	sec	sbc [<CtlPtr],y	cmp param	; look at new value	bcs @MaxOK	lda [<CtlPtr],y	; compute new max as Value+View.	clc	adc param	iny	iny	sta [<CtlPtr],y@MaxOK		;	jsr new_thumb	Compute new thumber.;	jsr scrollState	Is scroll bar drawable?	bcs exit1;;; ------- Compute area of old thumber needing to be erased ---------;	ldy #Thumb+x2	jsr CMsetrect2	Get rect of new thumber position.;	jsr SetUpColor	ldx <offset	lda <rect+y1,x	cmp <trect+y1,x	beq noerase	bcc skip2	cmp <trect+y2,x	bcs erase	sta <trect+y2,x	bra erase;skip2	lda <rect+y2,x	cmp <trect+y1,x	bcc erase	sta <trect+y1,x;;erase		; ;	lda #trect	Pass address of rect to FillRect.	jsr pushzpage;	ldy #PageRgnColor	Page region pattern	and color.	lda [<colorptr],y	tay	jsr set_patt	phx	Pass address of pattern.	phy	_FillRect	Erase thumber.;noerase		; ;;; ------- Draw new thumber -------------------------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldx #0	Normal falg.	ldy #CtlHilite	Is thumb highlighted?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$00FF	cmp #THUMB_PART	bne store	inx	Selected.	inxstore	ldy #state	txa	sta [<data],y	ldy #active	Must be active.	lda #0	sta [<data],y;	jsr draw_thumb	Draw thumber in new	position.	exit1	rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = =;        Given a new value, compute new	thumber for scroll bar.;;   IN:  Ctlptr = pointer to scroll bar.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = =	EXPORT new_thumbnew_thumb		;       ;;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldx #0	Offset for vertical	scroll bar.	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #DIR_SCROLL	beq store1	inx	inx	Offset for horizontal scroll bar.store1	stx <offset;;; --- Remember the old thumber ---------------------------;	ldy #PageRegion+x2	jsr CMsetrect2	rect = page region.;	jsr pushrect	jsr pushVvert_pen	pea 1	_InsetRect;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	ldx <offset	lda <rect,x	sta <front	Front side of page region.;	lda <rect+y2,x	Compute height of page region.	sec	sbc <rect,x	sta <height;;; --- Compute new RECT for thumber ----------------------------------;	ldy #Thumb+x2	jsr CMsetrect2	rect = thumber.;	ldx #x2	Save current thumber rect.lop2	lda <rect,x	sta <trect,x	dex	dex	bpl lop2;;; ------- Get size of thumber ----------------------------------------;	ldy #CtlData	op1 = view size.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	op1 = view size.	iny	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	op3 = total size of	data area.	ldy <height	op2 = size of page region.	jsr fraction;;; ------ Check minimum thumb size --------------------------------;	txa	ldx <offset	Horizontal or Vertical scroll bar?	beq ck_vermin;	ldy #min_thumb	cmp [<data],y	Minimum thumber size.	bcs store3	lda [<data],y	(Let it fall through, always 8 or more.);ck_vermin	cmp #8	bcs store3	lda #8;store3	sta <thumb_h	Number of pixels in	thumber.;;;	lda <height	Shrink page region by thumber size.	sec	sbc <thumb_h	sta <height;;; ------- Get starting position of thumber first --------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlValue	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	op1 = current value.	ldy #CtlData+2	lda [<Ctlptr],y	dey	dey	sec	sbc [<Ctlptr],y	op3 = data size - view size.	ldy <height	op2 = page height -	thumb height.	jsr fraction	phx	Number of pixels in	front of thumber.;;; ------- Update thumber rect ----------------------------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	lda #Thumb	clc	adc <offset	tay;	pla	Number of pixels in	front of thumber.	clc	adc <front	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	iny	iny	clc	adc <thumb_h	sta [<Ctlptr],y;	rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Move scroll bar.;;   IN:    param = delta y.;          param+2 = delta x.;;  OUT:    offset page and thumb RECTs.;;====================================================================move_bar	proc EXPORT	lda #Thumb	Offset thumber.	jsr offsetRect;	lda #PageRegion	Offset page region.;offsetRect	jsr pushrecord	pei <param+2	Pass delta x.	pei <param	Pass delta y.	_OffsetRect	Move the enclosing RECT.;	rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;                Setup to drag indicator.;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          colorptr	= pointer to control's color table.;;  OUT:    limit_blk initialized.;;====================================================================setup_drag	proc EXPORT;; --------- Perform	default setup ----------------------------------;	jsr setupcolor	Get control's color table pointer.;	ldy #PageRgnColor	Page region's color and pattern.	lda [<colorptr],y	tay	jsr set_patt	tya	ldy #drag_patt	sta [<data],y	iny	iny	txa	sta [<data],y;;; ---------- Clone page region for bounds and slop RECTs -----------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #PageRegion+x2	Get page region.	ldx #slop_rect+x2lop3	lda [<Ctlptr],y	phy	txy	sta [<data],y	ply	dex	dex	dey	dey	cpy #PageRegion	bcs lop3;	ldy #PageRegion+x2	Get page region.	ldx #bound_rect+x2lop4	lda [<Ctlptr],y	phy	txy	sta [<data],y	ply	dex	dex	dey	dey	cpy #PageRegion	bcs lop4;;; ---------- Compute bounds RECT from page region ------------------;	jsr pushbound_rect	jsr pushVvert_pen	pea 1	_InsetRect;;; ---------- Compute slop RECT from page region --------------------;	jsr pushslop_rect;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlFlag	Check directon.	lda [<Ctlptr],y;	ldy #$FFCE	50 pixels vertical slop.	ldx #$FFE7	25 pixels horizontal slop.	and #DIR_SCROLL	Vertical or horizontal?	beq store2	Equal if vertical scroll bar.;	ldy #$FFF0	16 pixels vertical slop.	ldx #$FFB0	80 pixels horizontal slop.;store2	phx	Pass horizontal slop to _InsetRect.	phy	Pass vertical slop to _InsetRect.;	ldy #GraphicsMode	320 or 640?	lda [<data],y	beq store3	If 320, I'm ready.;	lda 3,s	asl a	Double horizontal slop in 640.	sta 3,s;store3	_InsetRect;;; ---------- Set default movement axis -----------------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldx #2	Allow vertical flag.	ldy #CtlFlag	Check direction.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #DIR_SCROLL	beq store1	dex	Allow horizontal flag.store1	txa	ldy #axis_param	sta [<data],y		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Perform default reposition of indicator.;;   IN:    Ctlhand = handle of control.;          param = delta y.;          param+2 = delta x.;;  OUT:    offset page and thumb RECTs.;;====================================================================reposition	proc EXPORT	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	ldy #Thumb+x2	jsr CMsetrect2	rect = indicator.;	ldy #CtlFlag	Is it a vertical scroll bar?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	ldy <param	Y delta.	ldx <param+2	X delta.;	and #DIR_SCROLL	Is it a vertical scroll bar?	beq ckvert;	txy	Horizontal, change top and bottom.	ldx #x1	bra enter2;ckvert	ldx #y1;enter2	tya	Amount of change.	clc	adc <rect,x	New leading edge of	thumber.	tay	Save thumber leading edge.;	lda <rect+y2,x	sec	sbc <rect,x	pha	Size of thumber.	phy	Save new leading edge.;	phx	ldy #PageRegion+x2	jsr CMsetrect2	rect = page region.;	jsr pushrect	Less page region's border.	jsr pushVvert_pen	pea 1	_InsetRect	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	plx;	lda <rect+y2,x	sec	sbc <rect,x	Page region size,	sec	sbc 3,s	less size of thumber.	sta 3,s	op3 = page size - thumb size.;	pla	Get new leading thumb edge,	sec	sbc <rect,x	less page edge,	tax	op1 = number of pixels in front of thumb.;	ldy #CtlData+2	lda [<Ctlptr],y	op2 = data size,	dey	dey	sec	sbc [<Ctlptr],y	less view size.	tay	pla	Get op3.	jsr fraction	Compute proportion equation.;;; --- Set scroll bar's new value -------------------;	phx	Pass new value.	pei <Ctlhand+2	Pass control's handle.	pei <Ctlhand	_SetCtlValue;	rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Test to draw control.;;  OUT:    Carry set if control is invisible, inactive, or view >= data.;====================================================================scrollState	proc EXPORT	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlData	lda [<Ctlptr],y	Total view.	iny	iny	cmp [<Ctlptr],y	Total data area.	bcs exit	Everything in view?	sec	Don't draw flag.;	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #Ctl_INVIS	Is the scroll bar visible?	bne exit;	ldy #active	lda [<data],y	bmi exit	clc	exit	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************CheckForVis	PROC** This central routine checks the ctlFlag byte to see if* the invisible bit is set.  If it is clear, the routine* returns to the calling routine.** If the bit is set, this routine pops an extra word off* the stack and returns to the routine that called * the calling routine.*** Inputs:*	<ctlPtr** Outputs:*	returns or not** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	ldy #CtlFlag	Read the flag	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bit #ctl_invis	Are we visible?	beq @GoOn	Yes, go on	lda #0	Quit now.	tax	ply	Pull off extra RTS and go back to Ctl Mgr@GoOn	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************SetUpColor	PROC** Sets up colorPtr.*** In:    CtlHandle*        CtlPtr** Out:   ColorPtr* ** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 19 Feb 89	Steven Glass** This used to be part of ControlMgr.asm.  Now it is part* of DefProcs.  The change was made because the color table* ref was being made and memory manager calls could make* it move.  It was also being made too often.*****************************************************************;;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Start by copying the reference from the control record; to ColorPtr.  Who knows, it may even be right.;	ldy #CtlColor	Set pointer to the color table.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <colorptr	iny	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <colorptr+2;; If the control is not a super control, we are done.;	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	bpl @Done;; It is a super control.  See what the verb is.;	jsr ReadMoreFlags	and #ColorTableVerbMask	beq @Done		0 is pointer so all done	cmp #ColorTableIsHandle	beq @IsHandle@IsResource	pha	pha	PushWord #rCtlColorTable	pei ColorPtr+2	pei ColorPtr	jsr LoadResource	pla	sta ColorPtr	pla	sta ColorPtr+2;; memory may have moved, so reset ctlPtr;	jsr Dereference@IsHandle		ldy #2	lda [ColorPtr],y	tax	lda [ColorPtr]	sta ColorPtr	stx ColorPtr+2@Done		rts	ENDP	END